 "notes": "Single OCR sheet: overburden-thickness (isopach) map, explanatory text and three cross sections. Map face garbled: isopach contour labels and drill-site labels cannot be read or tied to contours, so no contour values or observations recorded. Section names, vertical exaggerations and units are read from the OCR layout (inferred). Map compiled from several hundred drill logs (USGS, SCGS, private firms); none are in the document.\nSUBSURFACE: the three sections (p.1) have vertical scales in ft and m (about -150 ft/-45 m to 300 ft/90 m) with a zero line whose datum is not printed in the OCR; distances and unit elevations along them are not legible. Top of bedrock (Cooper Formation) is very irregular in the southwest, with discontinuous limestone ledges; no elevations given. Map vertical datum not stated.",
